OL,3,GNEWSAWarning of blue-green algae at
OL,4,Acity park
OL,5,
OL,6,FTwo ponds in Hull's Queen's Gardens are
OL,7,Fbelieved to be infested with blue-green
OL,8,Falgae.
OL,10,FHull City Council said samples taken
OL,11,Ffrom the western side of the gardens
OL,12,Fwould be tested to determine if
OL,13,Fblue-green algae is present.
OL,15,FThe authority put up signs earlier to
OL,16,Fadvise visitors to avoid contact with
OL,17,Fthe water and to keep dogs on a lead
OL,18,Fand away from the ponds.
OL,20,FAccording to the Environment Agency,
OL,21,Fblue-green algae can be toxic to people
OL,22,Fand animals.
OL,23,APub: 19-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
